g down"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having left lying down"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"குறி","parts":[{"text":"குறி","lemma":"குறி","gloss":"trysting place"}],"gloss":"trysting place"},{"surface":"வந்தனென்","parts":[{"text":"வந்தனென்","lemma":"வந்தனென்","gloss":"I came"}],"gloss":"I came","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இயல்","parts":[{"text":"இயல்","lemma":"இயல்","gloss":"well-made"}],"gloss":"well-made"},{"surface":"தேர்","parts":[{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"தேர்","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"chariot"},{"surface":"கொண்க","parts":[{"text":"கொண்க","lemma":"கொண்க","gloss":"O lord of the maritime tract"}],"gloss":"O lord of the maritime tract","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செல்கம்","parts":[{"text":"செல்கம்","lemma":"செல்கம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செலவியங்","parts":[{"text":"செலவியங்","lemma":"செலவியங்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொண்மோ","parts":[{"text":"கொண்மோ","lemma":"கொண்மோ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அல்கலும்","parts":[{"text":"அல்கலும்","lemma":"அல்கலும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆரல்","parts":[{"text":"ஆரல்","lemma":"ஆரல்","gloss":"eel"}],"gloss":"eel"},{"surface":"அருந்த","parts":[{"text":"அருந்து","lemma":"அருந்து","gloss":"to eat"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"to eat"},{"surface":"வயிற்ற","parts":[{"text":"வயிற்ற","lemma":"வயிற்ற","gloss":"having stomachs"}],"gloss":"having stomachs","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நாரை","parts":[{"text":"நாரை","lemma":"நாரை","gloss":"heron"}],"gloss":"heron"},{"surface":"மிதிக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"மிதிக்கும்","lemma":"மிதிக்கும்","gloss":"will step on"}],"gloss":"will step on","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"மகள்","parts":[{"text":"மகள்","lemma":"மகள்","gloss":"daughter"}],"gloss":"daughter's"},{"surface":"நுதலே","parts":[{"text":"நுதல்","lemma":"நுதல்","gloss":"forehead"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphatic particle"}],"gloss":"indeed the forehead"}]}],"literal":"Having left the sand doll on the expanse of the coastal land, / I came to your trysting place, O lord of the well-made chariot! / Let us go, please undertake the journey, for every night, / having eaten the eel, with filled stomachs, / the herons will step on my daughter's forehead.","translation":"Leaving our sand doll behind on the coastal shore, I came to meet you at the trysting place, O lord of the swift chariot! Now let us return; please make your departure. For every night, the herons, their bellies full after feeding on eels, will trample upon the forehead of my dear girl's sand image.","modern":"நெய்தல் நிலத்து மணல் பரப்பில் நாம் செய்த பாவையை அப்படியே கிடத்திவிட்டு, நல்ல தேரையுடைய தலைவனே, உன்னைக் காண்பதற்காக உனது குறிப்பறிந்து வந்தேன். இனி நாம் செல்வோம்; நீயும் உனது பயணத்தை மேற்கொள்வாயாக. ஏனெனில், நாள்தோறும் ஆரல் மீன்களைத் தின்று வயிறு நிறைந்த நாரைகள், என் மகளாகிய இவளது நெற்றியைப் போன்ற மணல் பாவையை மிதித்து அழித்துவிடும்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the heroine's friend to the hero during a secret night-tryst. She urges him to marry the heroine soon instead of continuing these risky nocturnal visits. She explains that she left the heroine's sand doll on the beach to come and meet him, but they must now depart. The imagery of the heavy-bellied herons trampling the sand doll's forehead represents how the heroine's beauty and reputation will be ruined by public gossip if the hero delays their marriage. This coastal landscape (neytal tiṇai) imagery perfectly captures the anxiety of waiting and the threat of social slander.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}